@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - SYSTEM ADMINISTRATION: OPERATIONS</b>
  --
  <b>WATCH THE COMPUTE GRID</b>
  --
  <b>GRID SUMMARY</b> | sampled 14:31:02 | [ Refresh ]
  {
    Hosts 6 | (Online 5) | (Idle 2)
    Workunits 128 | Batches 9 | (Active 3)
    Outcomes today: (412 success) | (3 client error) | (1 no reply)
  }
  --
  <b>NODES</b>
  {#
    Node | Tasks done | Since last | Mean time | Fetched | Uploaded | Since heartbeat
    grid-01.example.com | 1284 | 12 | 42 s | 1.2 GB | 220 MB | 8 s
    grid-02.example.com | 903 | 4 | 38 s | 800 MB | 140 MB | 12 s
    grid-05.example.com | 101 | 0 | - | 40 MB | 2 MB | (3 h 12 m)
  }
  --
  <b>COMPUTE WRAPPERS</b> | 4 of 5 reported in the last five minutes | (1 missing)
  {#
    Instance | Status | Version | Last heartbeat
    6f2c19a1 | running | v0.0.25 | 8 s
    c47e5508 | running | v0.0.25 | 21 s
    b8d3a9e2 | running | v0.0.25 | 5 s
    42f0c7d1 | running | v0.0.25 | 11 s
    - | (missing) | - | -
  }
  --
  Read-only. The grid is the installation's: every tenant's work runs on the
  same hosts. A node whose last column grows is the one to look at; the node
  keeps its row while it is quiet. One wrapper runs on each node and takes the
  work that node runs, but nothing joins the two rows yet: a wrapper heartbeat
  carries no host, and a node sample carries no release.
  --
  [ Open the node ] - waits for the compute journeys
  --
  <b>NO SAMPLE YET</b>
  --
  The deployment stores no grid summary yet. The node table stands alone.
}

@enduml
